# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Unity generated
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/[Ll]ibrary/
/[Tt]emp/
/[Oo]bj/
/[Bb]uild/
/[Bb]uilds/
/[Ll]ogs/
/[Uu]ser[Ss]ettings/
/[Mm]emoryCaptures/
/[Rr]ecordings/

# Never ignore Asset meta data — Unity needs it to keep references stable.
!/[Aa]ssets/**/*.meta

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Asset Store / third-party drops
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
/[Aa]ssets/AssetStoreTools*
/[Aa]ssets/Plugins/Editor/JetBrains*

# Downloaded CC0 art is fetched per-machine by Tools > Grotto > Asset Fetcher.
# Keep the folder and its manifest, ignore the payload.
/Assets/Game/Art/Downloaded/*
!/Assets/Game/Art/Downloaded/.gitkeep
!/Assets/Game/Art/Downloaded/README.md

# Imported character models.
#
# Ignored by default, and this is a deliberate choice rather than an oversight.
# Whatever you download has its own licence, and a repository carrying redistributed
# model files — especially anything extracted from a shipped game — is a repository
# that cannot be published, put on itch, or handed to a collaborator. Keep the models
# on your machine and the credits in git.
#
# If every model you use is licensed for redistribution, delete these four lines.
/Assets/Game/Resources/Cast/Models/*
!/Assets/Game/Resources/Cast/Models/.gitkeep
!/Assets/Game/Resources/Cast/Models/CREDITS.md

